claim.claim-text:
1. A spectrum analysis system comprising:
at least one device including a processor and a memory configured to receive and analyze radiofrequency (RF) data including data relating to at least one signal; and
a data extraction module configured to receive spectral components of the at least one signal;
wherein the data extraction module is configured to determine a modulation type and a protocol based on the spectral components;
wherein the data extraction module is configured to organize the spectral components in a format based on user input;
wherein the at least one device is configured to determine signal degradation data for the at least one signal based on noise figure parameters of at least one second device emitting the at least one signal;
wherein the at least one device is configured to perform pattern distortion, generate propagation models, and generate next neighbor interference models using the signal degradation data; and
wherein the data extraction module is further configured to compare the spectral components of the at least one signal to previously stored signals in a database and store a match in the database when the comparison is positive and display an indication of a new unidentified signal when no match is found.

8. A spectrum analysis apparatus comprising:
at least one device including a processor and a memory configured to receive and analyze radiofrequency (RF) data of at least one signal; and
a data extraction module configured to receive spectral components of the at least one signal;
wherein the data extraction module is configured to organize the spectral components in a format based on user input;
wherein the at least one device is configured to determine signal degradation data for at least one signal based on environmental parameters, including rain, fog, and/or haze, and hardware parameters of at least one second device emitting the at least one signal, including antenna type, orientation, azimuth, gain, and/or effective isotropic radiated power (EIRP); and
wherein the data extraction module is further configured to compare the spectral components of the at least one signal to previously stored signals in a database and store a match in the database when the comparison is positive and display an indication of a new unidentified signal when no match is found.

14. A method for spectrum analysis, comprising:
analyzing by at least one device including a processor and a memory, radio frequency (RF) data to identify at least one signal;
receiving by a data extraction module, spectral components of the at least one signal;
determining, by the data extraction module, a modulation type and a protocol based on the spectral components;
organizing by the data extraction module the spectral components in a format based on user input;
determining by the at least one device, signal degradation data for the at least one signal based on noise figure parameters of at least one second device emitting the at least one signal;
performing pattern distortion, generating propagation models, and/or generating next neighbor interference models using the signal degradation data; and
wherein the data extraction module is further configured to compare the spectral components of the at least one signal to previously stored signals in a database and store a match in the database when the comparison is positive and display an indication of a new unidentified signal when no match is found.
